Privacy Policy for AI Guardian Web Shield

Local processing
The current extension analyzes webpage addresses, visible content, links and form metadata locally in your browser. It uses packaged heuristic rules. It has no telemetry, remote AI service, remote rule synchronization or browsing-data upload. The extension's packaged pages prohibit network connections through their content security policy. Visiting a website still makes that website's normal network requests; Web Shield does not make those requests private.

Data processed in memory
Page reports may contain the current page URL, domain, link URLs, visible page or email excerpts and risk explanations. Reports remain in service-worker memory for the tab and are cleared on navigation or tab closure; worker suspension also discards them. Do not treat memory as encrypted storage.

Connected Form Actions observes sign-in field types, whether a field was interacted with, effective form destinations and methods, and whether Guardian paused or allowed a submission attempt. It does not read form-field values. Its bounded in-memory history uses generated form IDs and URL origins, excludes paths, queries and fragments, expires after 90 seconds and resets on navigation. It cannot verify a completed network transfer or observe hidden agent tool calls.

Persistent local storage
Chrome local extension storage contains interface preferences, safety settings, site exception hosts, a salted passcode hash and salt, temporary unlock/cooldown deadlines, failed-attempt counts, and a bounded settings-change history. If you enter a trusted-adult review note, that note is also stored locally and may contain personal information. New history entries do not copy that note; existing copies in history are removed when this version starts. Site exceptions and their history can reveal website names. These records are not encrypted by Web Shield and are not sent by the extension to a trusted adult.

Content scripts on scanned pages receive only the preferences needed for analysis and display. They cannot directly read or write persistent extension storage, retrieve passcode records or review notes, or change protected settings through the service worker. Only the packaged extension controls can use those commands.

Retention and deletion
You can clear the trusted-adult note and remove site exceptions in the side panel. The settings history keeps up to 16 records, including previous exception hosts. Removing the extension removes its local extension storage through Chrome. A browser profile or device backup may retain copies according to its own settings. Protect your device and browser profile; a local numeric passcode is not a substitute for operating-system access controls or encryption.

Sharing and remote code
Web Shield does not sell or send the data described above to third parties. All analysis scripts are packaged with the extension. Browser installation, extension updates and GitHub support pages are handled by their respective providers under their own policies.

Limits and contact
Web Shield provides heuristic guidance and cannot guarantee that a page is safe or protect a compromised device. See SECURITY.md for the security boundaries. For support, visit https://github.com/AL91Cole/ai-guardian-web-shield. Do not post personal information, passcodes, page reports or real browsing history in public issues.

